rrows,\n41\tfoam, bubbles, and laundry-room surroundings. Reconstruct that visual design accurately throughout the existing stage.\"\n42\tSame for 05, 06, 07, 08 (each keeps its unique approved scenery). **Do not change the existing gameplay length, coin totals,\n43\tmovement rules, or transitions without the user's permission.** No more than TWO specialist agents actively working at once\n44\t(the reviewer runs only while a builder is paused). Show separate large APPROVED / BEFORE / NEW pictures proving the scenery\n45\tgenuinely looks closer. No generic replacements, no unnecessary redesigns. 01–03 / 09–11 = Google Flow videos.\n46\t\n47\t## User clarification ~03:25 UTC — REAL, CONSISTENT 3D (binding)\n48\t\"Do not simply move or stretch my approved picture in front of Benny to make it appear correct. Reconstruct the actual\n49\tvisual shapes, gold rings, scenery, water, foam, bubbles, materials, and lighting so they continue looking like my approved\n50\tartwork as Benny swims. I want the same beautiful visual appearance, not an illusion that breaks when the character moves.\"\n51\tRules derived (sent to both builders): world-fixed geometry only (nothing recalibrated from the camera / Benny per frame, no\n52\tsliding seams, no Benny-relative texture offsets); the painting supplies SHAPES and MATERIALS (world-anchored textures in each\n53\tobject's own UVs, or a fixed projector onto correctly shaped surfaces); every kept step passes a consistency check (forward,\n54\tsteering, through-screen views look like one coherent place with correct parallax).\n55\tDisclosed to the user: kept switches that are NOT real fixed 3D — 05 `m05ride` (painted water pattern laid out relative to\n56\tBenny), 05 `m05far` (far tunnel block recalibrated to the live eye every frame, sliding seam), 04 `m04room` (flat painted\n57\tbackdrop). They stay in the code (nothing deleted); the world-fixed reconstruction replaces them only when it looks at least\n58\tas close, and the user decides.